<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jakarta</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Jayakarta</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jakarta is the largest city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>, on the north-west coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a>. Its port, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunda-kelapa">Sunda Kelapa</a>, was taken by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatahillah">Fatahillah</a> in 1527 and renamed Jayakarta. In 1619 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a> seized it and built <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/batavia">Batavia</a>, its Asian headquarters and the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-indies">Dutch East Indies</a>. The city took the name Jakarta in 1942 and became the capital of independent Indonesia.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jakarta.jpg" alt="Jakarta" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Medelam · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bundaran_Hotel_Indonesia_(2025)_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
